  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197586",
      "title": "Introducing the Dimensions API",
      "lectureOrder": 81,
      "videoOrder": 78,
      "sourceHash": "0381548ae43499d871927c021dd947afb9bd41b7c865ea6104b1455a58675b85",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.68,
          "en": "So min and max width",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.68,
          "end": 7.2,
          "en": "and min and max height are useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.2,
          "end": 10.14,
          "en": "But sometimes you have problems that can't be solved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.14,
          "end": 12.94,
          "en": "with these properties alone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.94,
          "end": 15.46,
          "en": "And for this, let's get back here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.46,
          "end": 19.67,
          "en": "This overall UI on a small screen is okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.67,
          "end": 23.6,
          "en": "but everything is a little bit too big.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.6,
          "end": 27.19,
          "en": "We might wanna choose a smaller font size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.19,
          "end": 29.81,
          "en": "We might wanna choose less margin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.81,
          "end": 34.09,
          "en": "between this number container and this input box.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.09,
          "end": 37.13,
          "en": "We might want to make everything a little bit smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.13,
          "end": 41.01,
          "en": "because we know they we're on a smaller device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.01,
          "end": 43.093,
          "en": "Now, how can we do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.02,
          "end": 45.98,
          "en": "There might be different ways of achieving this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.98,
          "end": 48.57,
          "en": "but a great way of solving this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.57,
          "end": 52.79,
          "en": "is to use the built-in dimensions API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.79,
          "end": 55.45,
          "en": "Now for that, I'll go to this number container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.45,
          "end": 58.63,
          "en": "as an example, and there I wanna reduce the padding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.63,
          "end": 61.73,
          "en": "and the margin if we're on a smaller screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.73,
          "end": 63.74,
          "en": "and I wanna reduce that font size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.74,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "if we're on a smaller screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 68.73,
          "en": "And for this we can use this dimensions API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.73,
          "end": 70.91,
          "en": "And we use this dimensions API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.91,
          "end": 74.01,
          "en": "by importing it from react-native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.01,
          "end": 77.59,
          "en": "because it is an API built into react-native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.59,
          "end": 81.16,
          "en": "But it's not a component we would use in our JSX code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.16,
          "end": 83.22,
          "en": "instead it's a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.22,
          "end": 86.4,
          "en": "which we can use anywhere in our JavaScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.4,
          "end": 90.91,
          "en": "including our styles to get information out of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.91,
          "end": 92.42,
          "en": "Now which kind of information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.42,
          "end": 95.85,
          "en": "can we get out of the dimensions API?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.85,
          "end": 100.18299999999999,
          "en": "Well, for example, we can get the device width or height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.19,
          "end": 106.19,
          "en": "So here we could get the device width by using dimensions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.95,
          "end": 110.07,
          "en": "and then there is a get method which you can call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 113.46000000000001,
          "en": "And the get method takes an argument, which is a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.46000000000001,
          "end": 118.3,
          "en": "which holds either a value of screen or window.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.3,
          "end": 120.4,
          "en": "On iOS there is no difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.4,
          "end": 125.26,
          "en": "On Android, screen is the entire available width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.26,
          "end": 127.43,
          "en": "including the status bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.43,
          "end": 130.03,
          "en": "Window is excluding the status bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.03,
          "end": 132.11,
          "en": "So the actual part of the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.11,
          "end": 136.32999999999998,
          "en": "where the UI should be painted and usable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.32999999999998,
          "end": 141.32,
          "en": "So I will use window here to get that available device size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.32,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "And then on this object, which we get from this get method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 148.17000000000002,
          "en": "we can access various properties.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.17000000000002,
          "end": 149.64,
          "en": "We can access font scale",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.64,
          "end": 153.46,
          "en": "to find out which kind of scaling a user wants in the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.46,
          "end": 155.49,
          "en": "And you could then take this into account",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 155.49,
          "end": 159.32,
          "en": "and multiply your font sizes by that factor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.32,
          "end": 162.5,
          "en": "But here I'm interested in height and width.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.5,
          "end": 165.97,
          "en": "And we can, for example, get the width here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 165.97,
          "end": 168.34,
          "en": "and then use that in our styles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.34,
          "end": 169.723,
          "en": "But how can we use it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.62,
          "end": 174.27,
          "en": "Well for one, you could use it in mathematical calculations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.27,
          "end": 176.75,
          "en": "and say that the padding should be something like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 176.75,
          "end": 178.923,
          "en": "device width divided by 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.77,
          "end": 182.27,
          "en": "But what's probably more useful here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.27,
          "end": 184.58,
          "en": "is that you can use it in if conditions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.58,
          "end": 186.653,
          "en": "or ternary expressions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.51,
          "end": 191.31,
          "en": "We could say if the device width here is let's say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.31,
          "end": 195.41,
          "en": "smaller than 450 pixels,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.41,
          "end": 200.41,
          "en": "then we wanna use a padding of let's say 12,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.02,
          "end": 204.63,
          "en": "and we wanna use 24 if it's bigger than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 204.63,
          "end": 208.25,
          "en": "So on smaller screens we take a padding of 12 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.25,
          "end": 210.793,
          "en": "on bigger screens we take 24.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 211.87,
          "end": 216.44,
          "en": "If we save that you see the padding is reduced now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.44,
          "end": 218.03300000000002,
          "en": "it's now less here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.89,
          "end": 220.04,
          "en": "But it looks like here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 220.04,
          "end": 222.17000000000002,
          "en": "I actually chose the wrong break point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.17000000000002,
          "end": 225.02,
          "en": "because now on both devices, including the iPhone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.02,
          "end": 226.773,
          "en": "we have very little padding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.82999999999998,
          "end": 230.35,
          "en": "But if we find a better break point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.35,
          "end": 233.57,
          "en": "like 380 in my case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.57,
          "end": 236.15,
          "en": "then I have less padding on the left device",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.15,
          "end": 238.61,
          "en": "and more padding on the right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 238.61,
          "end": 241.23,
          "en": "We can also use this for the margin of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.23,
          "end": 246.23,
          "en": "So here then use the same formula or a different condition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.63,
          "end": 250.24,
          "en": "with different values for the margin,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 250.24,
          "end": 253.86,
          "en": "so that also the margin around this number container",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.86,
          "end": 256.04,
          "en": "is affected by that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 256.04,
          "end": 259.397,
          "en": "Now this gap here is not just the margin we set here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.397,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "therefore it's still pretty big,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 263.693,
          "en": "but will work on this gap soon as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 264.62,
          "end": 269.43,
          "en": "So that could be a useful tool for controlling some sizes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.43,
          "end": 270.54,
          "en": "And you could, for example now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 270.54,
          "end": 272.52,
          "en": "also use it here for the font size",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 272.52,
          "end": 276.33,
          "en": "and stick to 36 on bigger devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.33,
          "end": 280.64,
          "en": "but reduce this to 28 on slightly smaller devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.64,
          "end": 284,
          "en": "so that the font is a little bit smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284,
          "end": 288.78,
          "en": "compared to the device size than it is on bigger devices.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.78,
          "end": 292.2,
          "en": "Now, this is absolutely something you can play around with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 292.2,
          "end": 295.96,
          "en": "and you can adjust to your requirements and what you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 295.96,
          "end": 298.83,
          "en": "but you should be aware of this dimensions API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 298.83,
          "end": 301.21,
          "en": "which can help with finding out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 301.21,
          "end": 303.53,
          "en": "which available space you have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 303.53,
          "end": 306.75,
          "en": "to then adjust certain settings based on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 306.75,
          "end": 308.64,
          "en": "And it's up to you, whether you adjust",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.64,
          "end": 311.59,
          "en": "based on some if statement as we do it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.59,
          "end": 314.47,
          "en": "or if you have some dynamic calculation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.47,
          "end": 317.913,
          "en": "where the width or height is used as part of a formula.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 319.04,
          "end": 320.09,
          "en": "Now what I'll do here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 320.09,
          "end": 323.25,
          "en": "is I also wanna reduce this gap here a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 323.25,
          "end": 324.12,
          "en": "as I mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.12,
          "end": 327.283,
          "en": "And therefore what we can do is go back to the GameScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.23,
          "end": 330.36,
          "en": "and there it's the gap between the card",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330.36,
          "end": 331.823,
          "en": "and the number container.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.78,
          "end": 337.77,
          "en": "And here it's that margin to the top on the card",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 337.77,
          "end": 339.79,
          "en": "which I wanna change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 339.79,
          "end": 342.11,
          "en": "And therefore in this card component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 342.11,
          "end": 345.73,
          "en": "we can also include the dimensions API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 345.73,
          "end": 349.52,
          "en": "and then get our device with just as we did before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 349.52,
          "end": 354.42,
          "en": "with dimensions get window, and then the width.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.42,
          "end": 356.47,
          "en": "And then we can use this here for the margin top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 356.47,
          "end": 359.55,
          "en": "and check if this is smaller than 380,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 359.55,
          "end": 364.39,
          "en": "in which case the margin top maybe should just be 18 pixels",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 364.39,
          "end": 368.02,
          "en": "and otherwise it's 36 pixels.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 368.02,
          "end": 372.63,
          "en": "So now on smaller devices there's less margin to the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 372.63,
          "end": 376.33,
          "en": "And with that, we indeed did reduce this gap a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 376.33,
          "end": 377.71,
          "en": "on the smaller device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 377.71,
          "end": 381.28,
          "en": "and we still have the bigger gap on the bigger device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.28,
          "end": 385.74,
          "en": "Now, again, play around with it, find your favorite settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 385.74,
          "end": 389.72,
          "en": "and maybe adjust other components as well if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 389.72,
          "end": 393.34000000000003,
          "en": "I just wanted to introduce you to that dimensions API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 393.34000000000003,
          "end": 395.53,
          "en": "because it can be a useful tool",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 395.53,
          "end": 397.593,
          "en": "for situations like this here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
